   "created_at": "2026-10-27T19:55:18Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-10-27T19:55:18Z",
   "body": "The cards sent a bare npm name (`{\"spec\":\"opencode-cursor-auth\"}`), and `resolve` reads a bare name as one a community plugin goes by before npm's own, so npm's card installed `@magpie-community/opencode-cursor-auth`; the same bare name is refused with \"couldn't read the community plugin list\" when the market doesn't answer, because `npm:` is the form that reads no market.\n\nThis branch sends `npm:<name>` from every card -- the market's, a GitHub tag whose author published to npm, an npm search result, and the card page's Install -- for an npm package of a bare name. The community's scoped packages, folders and `github:owner/repo` specs are sent as they were, and the page's own field still resolves what a user types. `docs/subsystems/provider-plugins.md` records the rule.\n\n[fix/3928-gui-an-npm-card-installs](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3928-gui-an-npm-card-installs), commit 7f9586649e29cd7e3e3217f0ada8259ea8f42f46\n\nRan: `internal/gui/tests/plugin-npm-card-spec.test.cjs` (new, chromium and webkit) failed without the change (`actual 'opencode-kiro-auth', expected 'npm:opencode-kiro-auth'`) and passes with it; `plugin-market.test.cjs`, `plugin-local.test.cjs` and `plugin-git.test.cjs` pass. `plugin-github.test.cjs` fails \"de 440: a click scrolls nothing\" with the change reverted on `upstream/main` too. `gofmt -l`, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./internal/gui/` and `go test ./internal/gui/ -count=1` (459 passed) are clean.\n\nIt is a fork branch, ready for review; no claim on this issue.\n",
